**Crypto Dashboard Widget**

Below is a fully functional HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code for a live price ticker of the top 10 cryptocurrencies. This widget uses the CoinGecko API to fetch real-time data.

**HTML:**
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Crypto Dashboard Widget</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div class="widget-container">
        <h1>Top 10 Cryptocurrencies</h1>
        <table id="crypto-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Rank</th>
                    <th>Coin</th>
                    <th>Price (USD)</th>
                    <th>24h Change</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="crypto-data">
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

**CSS (in style.css file):**
```css
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    background-color: #f0f0f0;
}

.widget-container {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 40px auto;
    padding: 20px;
    background-color: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #ddd;
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
}

#crypto-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
}

#crypto-table th, #crypto-table td {
    border: 1px solid #ddd;
    padding: 10px;
    text-align: left;
}

#crypto-table th {
    background-color: #f0f0f0;
}
```

**JavaScript (in script.js file):**
```javascript
const cryptoTable = document.getElementById('crypto-table');
const cryptoData = document.getElementById('crypto-data');

const apiURL = 'https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/coins/markets?vs_currency=usd&order=market_cap_desc&per_page=10&page=1&sparkline=false';

fetch(apiURL)
    .then(response => response.json())
    .then(data => {
        data.forEach((coin, index) => {
            const row = document.createElement('tr');
            row.innerHTML = `
                <td>${index + 1}</td>
                <td>${coin.name} (${coin.symbol})</td>
                <td>$${coin.current_price.toLocaleString()}</td>
                <td>${coin.price_change_percentage_24h.toFixed(2)}%</td>
            `;
            cryptoData.appendChild(row);
        });
    })
    .catch(error => console.error('Error:', error));

setInterval(() => {
    fetch(apiURL)
        .then(response => response.json())
        .then(data => {
            cryptoData.innerHTML = '';
            data.forEach((coin, index) => {
                const row = document.createElement('tr');
                row.innerHTML = `
                    <td>${index + 1}</td>
                    <td>${coin.name} (${coin.symbol})</td>
                    <td>$${coin.current_price.toLocaleString()}</td>
                    <td>${coin.price_change_percentage_24h.toFixed(2)}%</td>
                `;
                cryptoData.appendChild(row);
            });
        })
        .catch(error => console.error('Error:', error));
}, 60000); // Update every 1 minute
```

**Example Use Case:**

To use this widget, simply save the HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code in separate files (e.g., `index.html`, `style.css`, and `script.js`) and open the `index.html` file in a web browser. The widget will display the current prices of the top 10 cryptocurrencies, along with their 24-hour price changes. The data will update every 1 minute.

